Here, the bases of the lower trapezoid are the same as those of the original trapezoid, but scaled down proportionally to the height. Specifically, if the original trapezoid has bases \(a\) and \(a + 100\), and height \(h\), then the lower trapezoid (which has height \( \frac{h}{2} \)) will have bases \( \frac{a}{2} \) and \( \frac{a + 100}{2} \).

